    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nGlenhest is a fine detached family home set in secluded and mature gardens of approx. 1 acre.\n\nGlenhest occupies a magnificent, secluded site extending to approximately an acre, offering a rare combination of privacy, scale and potential in one of South Dublin's most sought-after residential settings. \n\nHidden from view and surrounded by mature greenery, the property enjoys a peaceful, almost rural atmosphere while remaining close to a wide range of amenities.\n\nThe existing detached residence provides an excellent opportunity to create a truly impressive family home, with generous proportions and extensive grounds lending themselves to modernisation, extension or complete reimagining, subject to the necessary consents. \n\nAlso, on the site of this property is a separate two storey self contained unit (c.40sq.m) which would be ideal for older children or a nanny. There is also a spacious detached garage, providing ample storage and or space for a special car!\n\nThe gardens are a standout feature—expansive, private and well screened—offering exceptional outdoor space for family life, entertaining or quiet enjoyment.\n\nIn addition to its appeal as a private residence, the size and configuration of the site suggest future development potential would be possible, subject to obtaining planning permission.\n\nThis flexibility makes Glenhest an equally compelling proposition for owner-occupiers seeking space and seclusion, or purchasers with a longer-term vision for the site.\n\nGlenhest represents a rare opportunity to acquire a substantial holding in a discreet and highly convenient South Dublin location."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li>Impressive detached family home</li><li>Set on about an acre of mature gardens</li><li>Offering excellent potential to further develop (subj. to pp)</li><li>Ancillary accommodation </li><li>Next to Luas, excellent schools and M50</ul>"
      },
